  "content_blocks": [
    {
      "block_id": "b00000",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Procurement in an emergency",
      "ordinal": 0,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00001",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In: Plan > Strategy and plan",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00002",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Overview",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00003",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "This PPN is applicable to all contracting authorities, including central government departments, executive agencies, non-departmental public bodies, local authorities, NHS bodies and the wider public sector (collectively referred to as ‘contracting authorities‘).",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00004",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The PPN outlines options available when undertaking procurements in an emergency; and that may be considered in relation to procurements under the Public Contracts Regulations 2015 (PCR 2015), including:",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00005",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "call off from an existing framework agreement or Dynamic Purchasing System (DPS)",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00006",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "call for competition using a standard procedure with accelerated timescales",
      "ordinal": 6,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00007",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "extending or modifying a contract during its term",
      "ordinal": 7,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00008",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "direct award due to absence of competition or protection of exclusive rights",
      "ordinal": 8,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00009",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "direct award due to extreme urgency under regulation 32(2)(c) PCR 2015.",
      "ordinal": 9,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00010",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "It is important that contracting authorities continue to achieve value for money and use good commercial judgement and sound decision-making in an emergency, including when making direct awards.",
      "ordinal": 10,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00011",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Contracting authorities must keep sufficient documentation to justify decisions taken at all stages of the procurement procedure (as provided by regulation 84 PCR 2015: reporting and documentation requirements). This includes direct awards due to extreme urgency under regulation 32(2)(c).",
      "ordinal": 11,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00012",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Even though not required by regulation 32(2)(c), contracting authorities should consider some form of advertisement before making a direct award; running an informal competition and / or undertaking due diligence on the supplier market, for example.",
      "ordinal": 12,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00013",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Objective at this commercial stage",
      "ordinal": 13,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Objective at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00014",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In exceptional circumstances contracting authorities may need to procure goods, services and works urgently and without competition; where it is in the public interest to do so. In such circumstances there are a range of options available to contracting authorities.",
      "ordinal": 14,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Objective at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00015",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Key considerations at this commercial stage",
      "ordinal": 15,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00016",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Contracting authorities should:",
      "ordinal": 16,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00017",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "consider a range of commercial actions when responding to an emergency where it is in the public interest to act quickly. Various options are available if there is an urgent requirement for goods, services or works",
      "ordinal": 17,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00018",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "continue to achieve value for money and use good commercial judgement and sound decision-making in an emergency. These need to be managed in the context of the broader risk of not being able to secure the required goods or services in a timely manner. Potential risks are detailed further in the PPN (i.e. PPN 01/21)",
      "ordinal": 18,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00019",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "be aware that delaying or failing to do something in time does not make a situation qualify as urgent, unforeseeable or not attributable to the contracting authority",
      "ordinal": 19,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00020",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "keep proper records of decisions in line with regulation 84 PCR 2015. This means: documenting progress of procurement procedures, and; keeping sufficient documentation to justify decisions taken in all procurement stages.",
      "ordinal": 20,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00021",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Legal framework",
      "ordinal": 21,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00022",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The PPN should be read alongside the relevant parts of the legal framework, including but not limited to, the following provisions of the Public Contracts Regulations 2015 (which may be particularly relevant to the consideration of this PPN):",
      "ordinal": 22,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00023",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Regulation 27(5): Open procedure",
      "ordinal": 23,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00024",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Regulation 28 (10): Restricted procedure",
      "ordinal": 24,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00025",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Regulation 29 (10): Competitive procedure with negotiation",
      "ordinal": 25,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00026",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Regulation 32 (2)(c): Use of the negotiated procedure without prior publication",
      "ordinal": 26,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00027",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Regulation 33: Framework agreements",
      "ordinal": 27,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00028",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Regulation 34: Dynamic purchasing systems",
      "ordinal": 28,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00029",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Regulation 53(5): Electronic availability of procurement documents",
      "ordinal": 29,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00030",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Regulation 72: Modification of contracts during their term",
      "ordinal": 30,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00031",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Regulation 84: Reporting and documentation requirements",
      "ordinal": 31,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurement in an emergency",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
